i want to talk today about the phrase  trump derangement syndrome i've tweeted  about this  a few times and chauncey de vega wrote a  really good article about this on salon  which i tweeted yesterday  called there was no trump derangement  syndrome we were right about him  all along so let's talk about this trump  derangement syndrome  is a bad faith phrase which is meant to  shut down debate  stop conversation and excuse donald  trump's atrocious  behavior now i know that there will  certainly be some of you who will  respond to me and say you know david  look  check out this person on twitter who is  irrationally obsessed with everything  trump does and they think anything bad  in the world is trump's doing  this person is suffering from trump  derangement syndrome  listen you you can find instances of  everything on the internet but we're not  dealing in anecdotes here  the problem systemically with the phrase  trump derangement syndrome is that its  use is very  similar to what regressive left became a  couple of years ago i don't know if you  remember this  but regressive left much like trump  derangement syndrome are phrases that  are used to shut down debate  by disqualifying and dismissing  criticism  without actually having to debate the  merits of the criticism so  let's first really dig in i want  everybody to get this  what do people mean by trump derangement  syndrome the idea of tds  as it's sometimes called is to use it as  a retort  when someone criticizes donald trump  someone says look  trump did this trump's not responsible  for 160 000 deaths but he's responsible  for some because it's been one of the  worst responses to the virus  in the world you have trump derangement  syndrome and  what they mean by that is you are so  blinded by your hatred of donald trump  that we can dismiss  what you are saying without examining it  because you're just blinded by  by your rage against donald trump so  think back to the term regressive left  there was this very  very brief period where the term  regressive left  was sort of interesting in that it was  used to describe instances of ostensible  or supposed leftists failing to actually  be on the left in their views and  typically what what you had was  instances of people who claim to be on  the left being authoritarian and in a  sense it was a useful term for a very  short period of time and very quickly  the term regressive left  was bastardized and perverted by the  right and it became a catch-all  insult that they used to basically say  you're on the left and i don't like what  you have to say  i don't like what you're saying because  it's left wing and regressive left lost  all value as as any kind of a useful  tool  to explore failing to be on the left  trump derangement syndrome is equally  meaningless with the  important difference that unlike  regressive left trump derangement  syndrome  never actually described a real thing it  was always bogus there was a brief  period where regressive left actually  was an interesting  term to describe something i had been  talking about for for many years  which are instances of the authoritarian  left failing to really be on the left  but with each passing day the most  serious concerns about donald trump that  were expressed by people  on the left like me have been proven to  be true and they've been proven to be  true horrifyingly so remember that  months ago joe biden was widely  ridiculed for suggesting  you know trump might try to create some  kind of pretext an emergency of some  kind  to delay the election trump uh uh did  that  days ago by tweeting maybe we do need to  delay the election  joe biden was ridiculed and said he was  you know people were saying he has trump  derangement syndrome  he was right years ago people raised the  alarm  about donald trump's authoritarian  tendencies sort of he wants to be a  he's a wannabe dictator and over the  last month we have seen  him send armed paramilitaries to  american cities  to throw people into unmarked vans and  as chauncey de vega points out  points out in the article that we're  linking to which you should read quote  this was a phrase used to demean mock  reject  dismiss and deflect warnings about  donald trump's beliefs and tendencies  and those who were trying to raise the  alarm were called again as chauncey says  hysterical alarmist or out of touch  and bitter about hillary clinton's loss  if you encounter the phrase trump  derangement syndrome on the internet on  twitter  in real life maybe anywhere don't allow  yourself to be bullied into silence by  it  they claim on the right that they're all  about conversation  and yet this entire idea of trump  derangement syndrome is meant to stop  conversation make it clear that calling  someone a victim  of trump derangement syndrome is not  really an argument  say i'm glad to talk about that which  facts did i get wrong i'm glad to change  my views if you tell me what i got wrong  trump derangement syndrome is not an  argument it's a smoke screen it tries to  put us on the defensive  but the real derangement is the more  than 60 million people nearly 63 million  people who voted for donald trump in  2016 tens of millions of whom plan to  vote for him again  in just months that's the real  derangement  the horrifying nature of this presidency  which will be  affirmed by 50 60 65  67 million people who plan to vote for  it again  in november if there is any valid  criticism of those  like me on the anti-trump side it's that  we didn't do enough to raise the alarm  prior to him being elected as much as i  tried now  of course the people who are primarily  to blame are the people who  fell for it and voted for trump but if  you want to make a criticism of the  anti-trump left  that is to be taken more seriously  criticize us for something real  which is that as much as many of us were  trying to warn people  even we might have underestimated the  risks of the presidency  that's the reality trump derangement  syndrome don't allow it to be used  to silence actual critiques of this  president which if anything  have been not uh alarmist enough  let me know your thoughts i'm on twitter  at deepakman and remember you can get  the daily audio podcast  every day 3 pm eastern on your favorite  podcasting app whichever one it may be
 

